run
--rm
-i
--userns=keep-id
--name
apod-plain-proj-@PID@
--hostname
apod-plain
--secret
gh-plain,type=env,target=GH_TOKEN
-v
@TMP@/apod/plain/home:/home/agent:z
-v
@TMP@/apod/worklog/00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002:/run/apod-worklog:z
-v
@TMP@/mounts/ro1:@TMP@/mounts/ro1:z
-v
@TMP@/mounts/rw1:@TMP@/mounts/rw1:z
-v
@TMP@/mounts/cli-ro:@TMP@/mounts/cli-ro:ro,z
-v
@TMP@/mounts/cli-rw:@TMP@/mounts/cli-rw:z
-v
@TMP@/proj:@TMP@/proj:z
--tmpfs
/home/agent/.claude/sessions:rw,mode=1777,size=1m
-w
@TMP@/proj
--network
host
-v
apod-plain-nix:/nix
--label
apod.profile=plain
--label
apod.project=@TMP@/proj
--label
apod.session=00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
other-img
bash
-lc
gh auth setup-git >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; exec "$@"
_
claude
--permission-mode
bypassPermissions
--settings
{"permissions":{"deny":["mcp__claude_ai_Claude_Docs__*","mcp__claude_ai_UTS_Jitsu__*","mcp__claude_ai_Google_Docs__*","mcp__claude_ai_Google_Drive__*","mcp__claude_ai_Google_Sheets__*","mcp__claude_ai_Canva__*","mcp__claude_ai_Lovable__*","mcp__claude_ai_Notion__*"]},"hooks":{"PreToolUse":[{"matcher":"mcp__claude_ai_.*","hooks":[{"type":"command","command":"t=$(jq -r .tool_name); case $t in mcp__claude_ai_*) echo \"$t\" | grep -qE '^mcp__claude_ai_(Todoist)__' || { echo 'apod: connector not enabled for this run (apod -c)' >&2; exit 2; } ;; esac"}]}]}}
--session-id
00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
--append-system-prompt
You are running inside an apod container (podman), profile "plain". Only these host paths are mounted:
- @TMP@/proj (read-write, the project)
- @TMP@/mounts/ro1 (read-write)
- @TMP@/mounts/rw1 (read-write)
- @TMP@/mounts/cli-rw (read-write)
- @TMP@/mounts/cli-ro (read-only)
Nothing else from the host is available. There are no permission prompts: the container is the isolation boundary.
gh and git push over HTTPS use this profile's GitHub token.
Persistent volumes (kept between runs, not on the host filesystem): /nix.
Network: this pod shares the host's network (including Tailscale and services on the host's localhost).
claude.ai connectors enabled for this run: todoist. Others are blocked.
Work log: keep /run/apod-worklog/worklog.md up to date. It is kept on the host after this pod ends, and the user reviews it, across sessions, for work reports. After each meaningful step, append a few lines under a heading with today's date (## YYYY-MM-DD, a new one when the day changes): what you did, decided or found, what's blocked, what's next. Link PRs, issues and commits; facts, not narration; never secrets. Don't rewrite earlier entries.
-e APOD_PROFILE=plain
-e CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_AGENT_VIEW=1
-e GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=bot@example.com
-e GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Bot Agent
-e GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=bot@example.com
-e GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=Bot Agent
-e GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=6
-e GIT_CONFIG_KEY_0=url.https://github.com/.insteadOf
-e GIT_CONFIG_KEY_1=url.https://github.com/.insteadOf
-e GIT_CONFIG_KEY_2=url.https://github.com/.insteadOf
-e GIT_CONFIG_KEY_3=user.name
-e GIT_CONFIG_KEY_4=user.email
-e GIT_CONFIG_KEY_5=gc.worktreePruneExpire
-e GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_0=git@github.com:
-e GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_1=github.com:
-e GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_2=ssh://git@github.com/
-e GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_3=Bot Agent
-e GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_4=bot@example.com
-e GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_5=never
-e HOME=/home/agent
-e PLAIN=value
-e SOME_VAR=a b
